                        "review": "A decent game ruined by corporate greed.\r\n\r\nThe core game is genuinely good, and there’s a lot to enjoy in Dying Light 2. Unfortunately, Techland’s relentless monetization keeps dragging the experience down. The constant push to buy overpriced cosmetics is bad enough, with loading screens feeling more like advertisements than part of an actual game. And now they want to charge extra for spatial audio in their latest update? Seriously?\r\n\r\nAt some point, it stops feeling like a company supporting its game and starts feeling like a company squeezing every last penny out of its players. It’s a shame, because the game itself has a solid foundation, but these greedy practices make it difficult to respect the people behind it.\r\n\r\nMy advice? Stop rewarding this behavior with your money. If you absolutely want to play it, wait for a deep discount. Don’t pay full price just to be bombarded with monetization, and don’t encourage the idea that basic features and overpriced cosmetics are acceptable ways to milk a player base.\r\n\r\nSpeak with your wallet. The only language these companies seem to understand is money, and if enough players refuse to play along, they might finally reconsider these practices.\r\n\r\nYou have more power as a consumer than you think. Use it.",
